    "thesis": "Zscaler scores 58, a Hold, 7 points below the Buy line and 14 above Sell. Growth (73) and the balance sheet (100) are the strengths: revenue grew 24.88% year on year last quarter, and the company holds net cash with cash at 2.05 times debt. Quality (44) pulls the score down. The operating margin is -3.98%, stock-based pay equals 24.52% of revenue, and the share count rose 3.77%. The FCF margin is 14.09% once customer prepayments are stripped out, against 25.4% as reported. Valuation (37) is the weakest factor at 10.738 times sales and 76.196 times prepayment-adjusted FCF, although the stock has been cheaper in only 16.4% of the last 61 month-ends. Trend (61) and news (54) are middling: the price has rebounded 33.03% above its 200-day average but is still 34.34% below its 52-week high. Confidence is Medium because prepayments made up 34% of operating cash flow.",
